<title>NETHERLANDS: Dutch unadjusted unemployment falls in March-May.</title>
<headline>Dutch unadjusted unemployment falls in March-May.</headline>
<dateline>VOORBURG, Netherlands 1997-06-18</dateline>
<text>
<p>Dutch non-seasonally adjusted unemployment fell to an average of 381,000 in March-May from 399,000 in February-April, the Central Bureau of Statistics (CBS) said.  </p>
<p>DUTCH REGISTERED UNEMPLOYMENT NON-SEASONALLY ADJUSTED</p>
<p>			   March-May 97   Feb-April 97   March-May 96</p>
<p> total number	   381,000	  399,000	  441,000</p>
<p> pct of labour force    5.7		6.0		6.6</p>
<p>DUTCH REGISTERED UNEMPLOYMENT SEASONALLY ADJUSTED</p>
<p>			   March-May 97   Feb-April 97   March-May 96</p>
<p> total number	   385,000	  387,000	  446,000</p>
<p> pct of labour force    5.8		5.8		6.7</p>
<p>NOTES - Percentages are calculated in relation to average 1996 labour force (6.681 million). By international standards, the CBS uses a narrow definition of unemployment. Figures are compiled from job centre registrations and CBS survey.</p>
<p>The CBS said unemployment was continuing to fall at a rate of around 10,000 per month. It said the unadjusted figure of 381,000 was the lowest since December 1992.</p>
<p>-- Amsterdam newsroom, +31 20 504 5000</p>
